16153	{"artifactId":"LLD-59da3204a44afd1b-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-59da3204a44afd1b-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-12T10:10:12.557Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the Story's stated intent ('Paste images and attach documents in the dev chat prompt') and each of ac1, ac2, ac3 is designed.","evidence":"The only upstream record is the LLD's own JSON (.insrc/artifacts/LLD-59da3204a44afd1b-s1.json): meta.standalone=true, boundary.internal='Paste images and attach documents in the dev chat prompt', and acceptanceMapping names ac1/ac2/ac3 by id only. A search of .insrc for 59da3204 finds no SPEC/DEF/ISSUE carrying the text of those criteria or any non-goal list, so I could not compare the design against the criteria wording. The one-line intent itself (paste image, attach documents, chips, sent with the message, shown on the row) is designed in sections 2.2-2.5 and 3.4-3.5. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-59da3204a44afd1b-s1.json]","action":"Add the text of ac1-ac3 (and any non-goals) to the LLD or link the artifact that holds them, so the acceptance mapping can be checked against wording rather than ids.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The claude argv ends with `--` then the prompt, and the permission flags and --allowedTools are pushed before it, so `--add-dir` can go before the permission flags with the prompt still last (ref c1).","evidence":"cli-adapter.ts:489-504: args = ['-p','--output-format=stream-json','--verbose']; optional '--resume'; permission flags at 497-499; '--allowedTools' at 502; `args.push('--', req.prompt)` at 504. TurnRequest (44-63) has provider, prompt, resume?, cwd, permissionMode?, allowedTools? and no readDirs. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The codex argv also ends with `--` then the prompt and can stay unchanged.","evidence":"cli-adapter.ts:667-669: `['exec','resume',id,'--json',...auto,'--',req.prompt]` and `['exec','--json',...auto,'--',req.prompt]`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today a blank submit is a no-op, a malformed submit never throws, and runTurn has the stated signature; the shell's CSP already allows `img-src data:` (ref c2).","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:805-808: `async function runTurn(text: unknown, allowedTools?: readonly string[], opts?: { readonly suppressEcho?: boolean | undefined })`, `if (typeof text !== 'string') return;`, `if (prompt === '' || session === undefined) return;`. Line 488: csp = `default-src 'none'; img-src data:; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'nonce-${nonce}';`. Webview guard at 742: `function doSubmit(){if(!box.value.trim())return;...`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Invariant 'Every message kind is named in the protocol's type lists' is true of the code today (ref c3).","evidence":"protocol.ts:94 declares host->webview `{ type: 'approval-position'; ... }` and chat-panel.ts:262 posts it, but HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES (protocol.ts:221-231) lists only turn-event, session-restored, history-list, edit-prompt, docs-list, docs-content, user-row, theme, transcript-page. protocol.test.ts only asserts `.includes(...)` for chosen kinds; nothing pins the lists as exhaustive. So the lists are not a complete inventory today and a test can pass with a new kind left out. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts]","action":"Reword the invariant to what is true (the new kinds are added to the two lists and the protocol test asserts each by name), or add 'approval-position' to the list in this Story and say so. Do not rely on an existing exhaustiveness check: there is none.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Nothing for attachments exists yet in the plugin (no store, no message kinds, no readDirs / --add-dir).","evidence":"Case-insensitive search of vscode-plugin/src for 'attachment|chat-attachments' returns no files; search of cli-adapter.ts for 'readDirs|add-dir' returns no match. [files: vscode-plugin/src]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Reused pieces exist with the stated shape: sessionFileName(id), the output sweep's `{ olderThanMs, keep }` shape, PATHS.insrc in extension.ts, the store's onEvict hook, and vscode.d.ts declaring Uri.file and commands.executeCommand but not window.showOpenDialog.","evidence":"session-output.ts:176 `export const sessionFileName = (sessionId: string): string => sessionId.replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_-]/g, '_')`; :167 `sweep(opts: { readonly olderThanMs: number; readonly keep: ReadonlySet<string> }): Promise<void>`. extension.ts:16 imports PATHS, :448 `join(PATHS.insrc, 'chat-output')`, :455 `onEvict: (id) => void chatOutput.remove(id).catch(...)`, :460 sweep with `keep: new Set([...chatStore.list().map((c) => c.id), ...migratedChats.kept])`. vscode.d.ts:30-32 `Uri.file(path)`, :147 `executeCommand`, Uri has `fsPath` (:27); grep for showOpenDialog finds nothing. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-output.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts, vscode-plugin/src/vscode.d.ts]","action":"None. Note for the builder: the output sweep works on flat files grouped by suffix (session-output.ts:336-349), so the attachment sweep over directories is new code that mirrors its rule, not a call into it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The render registry exposes callback setters onApprovalDecision and onSelectionDecision on the returned object, so onAttachmentOpen can sit beside them, and toViewModel has a host copy and a webview copy.","evidence":"render-registry.ts:279 `var DEC=null;function onApprovalDecision(cb){DEC=cb;}`, :291 `var SDEC=null;function onSelectionDecision(cb){SDEC=cb;}`, :552 return object lists both; host toViewModel at :106-109, webview mirror at :350-353 (`if(entry.role==='user')return {kind:'user',role:'user',text:entry.text,collapsible:true};`). chat-panel.ts:640/643 wires the two setters to postMessage. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/render-registry.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The inventory of change sites for a blank-text submit with attachments is complete (the design lists doSubmit and runTurn).","evidence":"The host's 'submit-turn' case, chat-panel.ts:932-934, is not in the design: `if (typeof msg.text === 'string' && msg.text.trim() !== '') supersedeQueuedApprovals(); void runTurn(msg.text);`. supersedeQueuedApprovals (310-316) is what denies the in-turn request and clears the queue and grant chain when 'the user typed a message instead of answering'. With the design as written, a blank-text submit that carries attachments now runs a turn but skips this, so waiting approval cards and the grant chain survive a new user message. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"Add the 'submit-turn' case to the change sites: supersede queued approvals when the text is non-blank OR the session has pending attachments, and add that case to the host test for the blank-text submit.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"runTurn can keep its existing signature and still take the pending attachments only 'on a submit'.","evidence":"runTurn has three callers: the user submit (chat-panel.ts:934 `void runTurn(msg.text)`), the grant re-run (:363 `void runTurn(prompt, approvals.grantChain(), { suppressEcho: true })`) and the selection continuation (:1087 `void runTurn(`Selected: ...`, undefined, { suppressEcho: true })`). The design keeps the signature '(existing; behaviour extended)' and says the request carries readDirs 'including the synthesized grant re-runs', but never says how runTurn tells a user submit from the two synthesized calls. Built literally (runTurn drains the session's pending list), an Approve click or a selection confirm while the user has chips pending would attach them to a hidden synthesized prompt (suppressEcho, no user-row echo) and clear the chips. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"State the rule: only the 'submit-turn' caller takes pending attachments (e.g. an explicit opts field such as `attachments`, or drain in the submit-turn case and pass them in); the calls at :363 and :1087 pass none and only get readDirs. Add a host test that a grant re-run and a selection continuation leave the pending list untouched.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The live user-row echo and the title step are covered as change sites for the new field and for blank text.","evidence":"The echo is one post at chat-panel.ts:821 (`post({ type: 'user-row', text: prompt, key: ..., rowIndex: ... })`) consumed at :716 (`reg.appendKeyed(reg.toViewModel({role:'user',text:m.text}),m.key)`); the design names both ('user-row gains attachments', 3.5 lists chat-panel.ts and both toViewModel copies). Title: :826-830 derives from `prompt` and skips an empty clip (`if (derived !== '') s.title = derived;`), so the design's 'names the chat from its first attachment's name' is a real, needed change and is stated in 2.2. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"When building, pass the same fallback name to applyTitle(s, prompt) at :830, which would otherwise ask the title CLI call about an empty prompt.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The file store writes and reads a row as whole JSON, so an extra `attachments` field on a user row round-trips with no store change and old rows read as before.","evidence":"session-file-store.ts:134 `const rowLines = (rows) => rows.map((r) => `${JSON.stringify(r)}\\n`).join('')`; :199 `rows.push(JSON.parse(line) as TranscriptEntry)` with no per-field filter; :425 `plain = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(v))`. session-store.ts:30-37 user row is `{ role, text, cssClass?, at }`, so an optional field is additive. The older webview toViewModel reads only entry.text for a user row (render-registry.ts:353), so it ignores the field. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-file-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/render-registry.ts]","action":"None. Note the user row shares its union member with 'assistant' | 'marker' (session-store.ts:32); the type change should keep `attachments` optional there or split the user member.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A session's attachments directory can be keyed and cleaned exactly like its output files: same sessionFileName, same onEvict hook, same keep set at start.","evidence":"session-file-store.ts:129 uses `${root}/${sessionFileName(id)}` and calls `deps.onEvict?.(head.id)` at :308; extension.ts:455 and :458-461 show the output remove-on-evict and the start-up sweep with the store ids plus migratedChats.kept, both with `.catch` that logs. The attachments root (chat-attachments) is separate from chat-output, so the existing suffix-based sweep never sees the new directories. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-file-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Awaiting in-flight attachment writes before the submit is safe with how runTurn and the message handler work today.","evidence":"Today runTurn does everything up to the request synchronously after capturing `const s = session` (chat-panel.ts:805-812), and 'new-chat' / 'open-chat' reassign `session` (:957, :976). The design adds an await before the row is pushed ('Attachments still being written when the user submits are awaited first') but does not say which session is captured, or what happens if the user switches chat or a second submit arrives during that wait. I found no statement or test for it in the design; the code has no existing pattern to compare against because there is no await on this path today. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"State that the session and its pending list are captured before the await and the turn runs on that session, and say what a second submit or a chat switch during the wait does. Add it to the 'submit waits for an attachment still being written' host test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Failures of evict-time removal and the start-up sweep can be logged and not thrown, as for the output files.","evidence":"extension.ts:455 `onEvict: (id) => void chatOutput.remove(id).catch((e) => panelLog.warn(...))` and :458-461 `void chatOutput.sweep(...).catch((e) => panelLog.warn(`chat output sweep failed: ...`))`; the same pattern is available for the attachment store. session-output.ts:330-331 shows a missing root (ENOENT) is treated as nothing to sweep. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-output.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion maps to at least one test the gate can run, in the framework the plugin already uses.","evidence":"The mapping gives ac1 two gate tests (shell script; host pending list), ac2 two gate tests (host submit; claude argv) plus one live test, and ac3 one gate test (render registry) plus one smoke test. The named suites exist: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts, protocol.test.ts, session-output.test.ts use node:test with injected fakes. Every subject in the mapping appears verbatim in the test levels. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts]","action":"ac3's 'a click opens it' is proved in the gate only up to the registry sink; the host test 'open-attachment opens the resolved path' exists in the strategy but is not in ac3's mapping. Add it there so the open path is gate-proved and not smoke-only.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":3,"low":13,"unverified":2},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-12T10:10:12.557Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
